martin scorsese's 2010 feature shutter  island is a gripping psychological  thriller with one twist after another  it's also the second highest grossing  movie of the director's career at first  the film appears to tell the story of  teddy daniels he's a us marshal  investigating the disappearance of a  patient named rachel salondo from a  mental hospital located on shutter  island an isolated outpost in boston  harbor for this case teddy is working  with his new partner chuck all while at  the hospital teddy begins experiencing  hallucinations nightmares and migraines  everything is strangely off in a way he  doesn't understand he goes deeper and  deeper down a rabbit hole of madness  until he finally confronts dr colley who  runs the shutter island facility cauley  explains to him that he's not really  teddy daniels instead he's andrew leytus  a traumatized man who killed his wife  after she drowned their three children  the disappearance teddy believes he's  been investigating has actually been an  experimental treatment to cure him of  his manic delusions the shutter island  doctors hope that by indulging latest  belief he is teddy daniels he'll be able  to come to the conclusion on his own  about what really happened and accept  what he did throughout this treatment  the hospital staff has been  participating in the elaborate charade  and chuck teddy's supposed partner isn't  even a us marshal don't you recognize me  andrew  i've been your primary psychiatrist for  the last two  years one of the great things about  shutter island is that it's a very  different experience watching the movie  with knowledge of the twist versus not  knowing the second time watching it you  can see all the ways scorsese hints at  what's really happening before it's  revealed in fact there are subtle clues  in the first few minutes of the film  while taking the ferry to shutter island  teddy is throwing up in the bathroom  which he thinks is because he's seasick  actually it's because he's withdrawing  from his medication and the ocean  reminds him of the water in which his  wife drowns her children then he goes up  to the deck and meets chuck his new  partner teddy doesn't seem to think it's  weird that he's meeting him for the  first time on deck logically they would  have gotten on the ferry together since  the film doesn't make a point of  underlining how strange teddy and  chuck's introduction is it's easy to  accept it as normal event but it's the  first bit of foreshadowing that things  are not what they seem at shutter island  and something is very off with teddy  there are other intriguing hints about  the shutter island twist contained in  the opening scene one such moment is  when teddy doesn't have a cigarette  lighter as a patient he's probably not  allowed to have one because it's a  dangerous item additionally the boat's  bathroom area looks suspiciously like  the kind of cell where a patient living  in a 1950s institution would be held but  it's the meeting of chuck and teddy that  should immediately tip off viewers that  something strange is afoot looking back  on the film numerous other clues lead up  to the big twist it's a movie that  rewards multiple viewings and you'll  realize certain moments come across  differently with the knowledge of  teddy's true identity for instance when  teddy and chuck first arrive on the  island the guards seem to tense up and  grip their rifles a little tighter  initially audiences may think that there  are secrets on the island they need to  protect in actuality the guards are  nervous because they know teddy's one of  the patients and they don't know if he  could snap at any second however the  biggest clue you might have missed  occurs when the us marshals are asked to  relinquish their guns there's a  prolonged moment where chuck fumbles  getting his firearm out of its holster  if he were actually an experienced  marshal he should have no problem  getting it undone the reason he has an  issue is that he's really a doctor and  he doesn't know how to handle a gun  properly at first the scene comes across  as amusing but it gives up the entire  twist right there with all this in mind  it just goes to show what a master  filmmaker martin scorsese is he hid all  of these clues in plain sight yet most  viewers were still taken by surprise  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

